              "uri": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHlSXFxdVddXkZO-4XTFxdk_Pv_eZM5WOiziudZ80im0eFQ9hPvr5Qf7QYIPvrdKfOE9fAQonnkuIFN6IiRTceRBhRtQhjaJBgiTcYiBAKSNmkS92GHzGyAYXTeEtqv27DfMR09dXd2_N93T6VgY7bHHBNq-lmVPxiQx1zKKo6PNGiL8sFInGMEZwUI_L0zWjh-Mll8QCrruj2m6eGZzfJFFrBrbEyY29y6Gycz6Ex-7KYclVWyxs4qn5QO8QElI4bDAdey-6W2tGxh7Q=="
            }
          }
        ],
        "grounding_supports": [
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 693,
              "end_index": 792,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "However, their legal duties continue, specifically to cooperate fully with the appointed liquidator"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              1,
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 794,
              "end_index": 878,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Failure to cooperate can result in court orders, fines, or even a warrant for arrest"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 880,
              "end_index": 1000,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Directors are typically required to provide information and documents and attend meetings as requested by the liquidator"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              2,
              3,
              4
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1007,
              "end_index": 1163,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Investigation into Conduct**:\n    The liquidator is legally obliged to investigate the conduct of all directors in the period leading up to the insolvency"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              4
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1165,
              "end_index": 1298,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This investigation aims to establish the causes of the company's failure and identify any instances of misconduct or wrongful trading"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              3,
              5
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1300,
              "end_index": 1442,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The liquidator reports their findings to the Secretary of State, which can influence decisions regarding director disqualification proceedings"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6,
              7,
              8,
              9
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1449,
              "end_index": 1654,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Disqualification from Acting as a Director**:\n    If a director's conduct is deemed \"unfit,\" they can be disqualified from acting as a director for a period ranging from 2 to 15 years under the CDDA 1986"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              1,
              8
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1656,
              "end_index": 1881,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Grounds for disqualification include persistent breaches of company law (such as failing to file accounts or returns), fraudulent trading, wrongful trading, or not acting in the best interests of the company and its creditors"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1883,
              "end_index": 1995,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "A disqualification order also typically includes an order for the director to pay the Secretary of State's costs"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6,
              10
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1997,
              "end_index": 2194,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Breaching a disqualification order or undertaking is a criminal offence, potentially leading to a fine, up to 2 years in prison, and personal liability for company debts incurred during that period"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              10
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2196,
              "end_index": 2303,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "A compensation order may also be made against a disqualified director to repay losses suffered by creditors"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              12,
              4
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2330,
              "end_index": 2502,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Directors can be held personally liable for company debts and losses in several specific circumstances, effectively \"lifting the corporate veil\" that normally protects them"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2504,
              "end_index": 2594,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The IA 1986 provides the primary mechanisms for liquidators to pursue directors personally"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              13,
              3,
              5
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2645,
              "end_index": 2885,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Wrongful Trading (Section 214 IA 1986)**:\n    This civil offence occurs when a director continues to trade the company when they \"knew or ought to have concluded that there was no reasonable prospect of avoiding insolvent liquidation\""
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              13,
              9,
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2887,
              "end_index": 3009,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The duty of directors shifts from shareholders to creditors when a company becomes insolvent or is bordering on insolvency"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              15,
              3,
              9,
              5
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3011,
              "end_index": 3124,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Directors are expected to take \"every step\" to minimise potential loss to creditors once insolvency is recognised"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              13,
              16
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3126,
              "end_index": 3248,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "If found liable, a court can order the director to personally contribute to the company's assets to reduce creditor losses"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              3
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3250,
              "end_index": 3340,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This does not require proof of intent to defraud, only a failure to act with due diligence"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              16,
              9,
              14,
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3343,
              "end_index": 3561,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Fraudulent Trading (Section 213 IA 1986)**:\n    This is a more serious civil and criminal offence, requiring proof that the business was carried on \"with intent to defraud creditors or for any fraudulent purpose\""
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              16
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3563,
              "end_index": 3594,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This involves actual dishonesty"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              2,
              16,
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3596,
              "end_index": 3788,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Consequences for fraudulent trading can include an order to personally contribute to the company's assets, director disqualification, an unlimited fine, and a prison sentence of up to 10 years"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              0,
              9
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3791,
              "end_index": 4073,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Misfeasance and Breach of Duty (Section 212 IA 1986)**:\n    A liquidator can pursue directors if they have \"misapplied, retained, or become accountable for any money or property of the company,\" or have been \"guilty of any misfeasance or breach of any fiduciary or other duty\""
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4075,
              "end_index": 4246,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This includes actions such as paying unlawful dividends, making excessive salary payments, misapplying company assets, or making preferential payments to connected parties"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4248,
              "end_index": 4412,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The Supreme Court's \"creditor duty\" confirmed that directors must consider, and give effect to, the interests of creditors when insolvency is probable or inevitable"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              9,
              20,
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4414,
              "end_index": 4541,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "If a misfeasance claim is successful, the director may be ordered to repay or restore company property or compensate for losses"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              21
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4544,
              "end_index": 4662,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Personal Guarantees**:\n    Many directors provide personal guarantees to lenders (e.g., banks) for company loans"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12,
              22,
              21,
              4
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4664,
              "end_index": 4790,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "If the company enters liquidation and cannot repay the loan, the director will be personally liable for the outstanding amount"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12,
              4
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4792,
              "end_index": 4882,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This can lead to personal bankruptcy and the loss of personal assets, including their home"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12,
              4
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4885,
              "end_index": 5173,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Overdrawn Director's Loan Account (ODLA)**:\n    If a director has taken more money from the company than they have put in, resulting in an overdrawn director's loan account, this amount becomes a personal liability that the liquidator will seek to recover as an asset of the company"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              9,
              19
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5176,
              "end_index": 5460,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Transactions at an Undervalue or Preferences (Sections 238 & 239 IA 1986)**:\n    Liquidators can seek to reverse transactions where company assets were disposed of at less than fair market value or where certain creditors were preferentially paid in the period before insolvency"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              9
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5462,
              "end_index": 5585,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "If a director was involved in authorising such transactions, they could be ordered to restore the assets or repay the funds"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              9
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5587,
              "end_index": 5707,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "For transactions at an undervalue, insolvency is presumed if the transaction occurred within two years before insolvency"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              23,
              24
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5710,
              "end_index": 6041,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Re-use of a Prohibited Company Name (Sections 216 & 217 IA 1986)**:\n    It is a criminal offence for a director of a company that has gone into insolvent liquidation to re-use the company name (or a name so similar as to suggest an association) for another business within 5 years of the liquidation, without court permission"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              23
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6043,
              "end_index": 6133,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "A director who breaches this can become personally liable for the debts of the new company"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              12,
              21,
              5
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6490,
              "end_index": 6623,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Seeking professional insolvency advice early is crucial to navigate these complex challenges and minimise potential negative outcomes"
            }
          }
        ],
